WEBVTT

00:07:28.516 --> 00:07:31.196
to this Jurassic giant
that we're excavating.

00:07:31.236 --> 00:07:32.556
Pretty phenomenal.

00:07:32.556 --> 00:07:35.276
And this ichthyosaur,
I should say, that Nigel's holding,

00:07:35.316 --> 00:07:38.316
this is actually of a species
I named after him a few years ago,

00:07:38.356 --> 00:07:40.116
called Ichthyosaurs larkini.

00:07:42.116 --> 00:07:43.596
Whilst on site,

00:07:43.636 --> 00:07:45.356
one of the team members, Steve Dey,

00:07:45.356 --> 00:07:48.796
created a wonderful photogrammetry model,

00:07:48.836 --> 00:07:51.156
which, photogrammetry
is an interesting technique

00:07:51.196 --> 00:07:52.916
where you take thousands of photos

00:07:52.956 --> 00:07:55.676
and put them together and build
a three-dimensional model.

00:07:56.356 --> 00:07:58.516
Now what you're looking at
first of all here,

00:07:58.556 --> 00:08:01.236
is a base model that we made
back in February.